  "id": "mental-load",
  "term": "mental load",
  "definition": "Mental load is the burden of invisible household or caregiving work, especially the ongoing planning, organizing, and remembering that happens in the mind rather than through visible tasks. It is often described as constantly thinking about what needs to be done and feeling that the tasks are never fully finished.",
